    ],
    "summary": "The daemon's parser for the run request accepts the empty string as prompt when a kind of source is stated, and refuses it with 'invalid-params' and a message that says a kind of source must be stated when none is. A prompt of only white space is accepted with and without a stated source and is handed on untrimmed. The tests call the daemon's run handler; the accepted requests run for real over a sandboxed graph store and end at the indexed check with an intent that has no focus. Six mutations were each caught, among them treating white space as empty at the parser. Only the daemon's parser changed: no client or plugin was touched.",
